<title>ESTONIA: MICROLINK TO LAUNCH CABLE PRODUCTION.</title>
<headline>MICROLINK TO LAUNCH CABLE PRODUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microlink, the largest computer assembly group in the Baltics, will start the production of computer cables in June, Aripaev newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Microlink plans to have a monthly turnover of four million kroons, Hanno Haamer, chairman of Microlink Invest, was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>For the first two years the company will provide subcontracting services to Amphenol, one of the world's leading producers of electronic components, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
